&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Key Account Manager (KAM) is a field-based expert, that strategically drives the commercial objectives of selected genetic programs for Germany in the assigned territory. The KAM will be accountable for developing and implementing key account plans in their designated territory to optimize care for patients. The Key Account Manager, reporting to the Area Sales Lead, is expected to develop territory specific strategic account plans in the context of the overall product strategy and in close alignment with functions of Medical Affairs, Patient Advocacy, Market Access and Commercial, while ensuring full compliance with the relevant company, industry, legal, regulatory and ethical standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present a positive image of the company and develop awareness of Alnylam’s RNAi platform with relevant groups of healthcare professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, own, and drive territory and account plans, including customer targeting and cycle plan, in line with Marketing strategy and Business Operations guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve pre-launch and post-launch KPIs, including sales and volume targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use advanced sales skills to ensure consistent and continuous messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed analysis of the assigned territory to identify, assess, and develop relevant centers for diagnosis and treatment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive patient group identification, diagnosis and referral rates by strategic intersectoral referral network management in close cooperation with other field based functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop trusted relationships with a portfolio of customers to ensure market penetration, after developing a thorough understanding of key customer needs and requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the correct products and services are delivered to customers in a timely manner by collaborating with internal stakeholders (commercial, supply chain, and compliance) and external centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain contact with key customers and provide commercial and scientific services to ensure access at site of care, and that logistics are in place to administer product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and execute local meetings to drive diagnosis and treatment rates, in collaboration with the Medical Affairs Team for physicians and other healthcare professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Alnylam at local and national events and congresses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the link of communication between key customers and internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise and collaborate with relevant internal staff (Medical Affairs, Sales Director, Marketing, Market Access and Business Operations), as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steer regular local alignment meetings with other field based functions to ensure proper implementation and outcomes against the committed territory and account plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely and accurate reporting and continuous diligent maintenance of the CRM database&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct all activities to highest ethical standards in accordance with country code of practice and local Laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant domestic travel and occasional international travel as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;University degree in a business-related field such as health or business management or comparable educational background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified to promote medicinal products to national code of practice standard in Germany&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of Sales and Key Account Management experience in bio/pharmaceutical sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to gain consistent access and develop strong &amp;amp; professional relationships for product promotion with healthcare providers in reference centers and the community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and influencing skills to engage with professionals at all organizational levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen to add value to the existing health care structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to draw on previous experiences and insights to generate and maintain appropriate awareness and timely access to treatment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German and English, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel within a territory on a regular basis (80% of the time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam: &lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;At AutoProff, we&#39;re looking for a new colleague&amp;nbsp;to help manage and develop our supplier and transport network across Europe. This is a hands-on role with a mix of operational and commercial responsibilities, where you&#39;ll work closely with suppliers and colleagues across the business to ensure our operations run smoothly and efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our new Senior Transport Manager, you will be responsible for managing supplier relationships, monitoring operational performance, and ensuring our supplier and transport network supports our business across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with internal teams and external suppliers to ensure reliable supplier performance, support day-to-day operations, and identify opportunities to improve the way we work. While you&#39;ll be involved in supplier and transport contracts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with &lt;strong&gt;AutoScout24&#39;s Procurement team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;,&lt;/strong&gt; who lead the commercial negotiations and sourcing activities, ensuring a consistent procurement approach across the group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position can be based at our headquarters in &lt;strong&gt;Vejle, Denmark&lt;/strong&gt;, or at our office in &lt;strong&gt;Düsseldorf, Germany&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Let&#39;s dive into your key responsibilities, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the daily collaboration with suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor supplier performance and service level agreements (SLAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up on delayed orders and resolve operational issues together with suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate transport vendors to ensure efficient logistics operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain supplier rebate and kickback agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approve supplier invoices in Coupa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support claims and handle supplier escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure suppliers comply with contractual agreements and internal processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve processes and reduce costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain supplier data, dashboards, KPIs, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Procurement, Operations, Finance, Customer Support, and other internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The need-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of experience in Supplier Management, Procurement, Logistics, Transport Management, or a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with transport providers and logistics operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing supplier performance and service level agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to use data to support decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with ERP or procurement systems (experience with Coupa is an advantage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage several tasks and priorities at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in English and German or Danish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The nice-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience from an international technology, marketplace, automotive, or e-commerce company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with transport sourcing and freight procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling supplier claims and disputes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with dashboards and KPI reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will thrive in this role if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy working with both operational tasks and commercial discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build good working relationships with suppliers and colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Like solving problems and finding practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a structured way and follow tasks through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable taking responsibility and making decisions within your area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you think we could be a match, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About AutoProff&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AutoProff was founded in 2013 by the experienced car dealer Jesper Ratza in Denmark. The aim was to digitalise B2B used car trading, helping car dealers increase sales and improve profits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;in August 2022, AutoScout24, the leading specialised pan-European online car marketplace, acquired a majority stake in AutoProff. The partnership has supported the rapid expansion of AutoProff&#39;s solutions across Europe and enables the creation of Europe&#39;s first fully integrated C2B-B2B-B2C dealing solution for used cars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At AutoProff, we specialise in providing online B2B used-car dealing solutions designed to improve the buying and selling experience for professional car dealers and their customers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With a focus on effective solutions, digitisation and customer service, we are committed to being the home of B2B car dealing for European dealers, including trade-ins cars, retail-ready cars, newer used fleet vehicles and insurance write-offs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are the emerging European leader with more than 150,000 B2B used cars on our online trading platforms annually. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior FP&amp;amp;A Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Finance&lt;/strong&gt; team based in &lt;strong&gt;Paris&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior member of our Paris HQ Finance team, the Senior FP&amp;amp;A Analyst holds the full view of the company P&amp;amp;L, from net sales to EBITDA, across all channels and regions. The role combines ownership of the planning and reporting cycles with hands-on business partnering, and plays a central part in structuring our FP&amp;amp;A processes as the brand scales internationally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a rigorous, process-oriented finance professional with a strong retail background and a sharp understanding of margin mechanics. You are comfortable owning the numbers end to end and challenging the business on what drives them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;full-time permanent position (CDI)&lt;/strong&gt; based at our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;em&gt;with 4 days per week in the office and 1 day of remote work possible&lt;/em&gt;). The role reports to the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Finance&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full P&amp;amp;L ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; own the company-wide P&amp;amp;L view, from net sales through gross margin, store contribution and operating expenses down to EBITDA, consolidated across retail, e-commerce and wholesale, and across the US, Europe and Asia. Act as the go-to reference on P&amp;amp;L performance and its drivers for the Head of Finance and the leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budgeting &amp;amp; forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; lead the annual budget, monthly reforecasts and long-range plan. Own the planning calendar, key assumptions and models, and consolidate inputs from regional and functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Margin management:&lt;/strong&gt; own margin analysis at every level (channel, market, category, collection, SKU), including markdowns, promotions, cost of goods, freight, duties, FX and inventory provisions. Build margin bridges, explain variances and drive recommendations on pricing and markdown strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monthly close &amp;amp; reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; own the FP&amp;amp;A month-end close and the global management reporting package (actuals vs. budget, forecast and prior year, variance commentary, KPI dashboards). Work with Accounting to ensure management and statutory figures reconcile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business partnering:&lt;/strong&gt; serve as finance partner to Retail, E-Commerce, Wholesale, Merchandising and Supply Chain leaders on store P&amp;amp;Ls, inventory productivity and open-to-buy, pricing, promotional plans, and business cases for store openings and market entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processes &amp;amp; controls:&lt;/strong&gt; design, document and continuously improve FP&amp;amp;A processes, templates, review controls and data standards. Drive reporting automation across the finance stack (NetSuite, Excel / Google Sheets, BI tools) in coordination with Accounting and IT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership support:&lt;/strong&gt; prepare materials for executive and board reviews and lead ad hoc analyses requested by the CFO and the Head of Finance. Review and guide the work of junior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5–7 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in FP&amp;amp;A, controlling or financial planning, with significant exposure to a company-wide or business-unit scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail experience is mandatory:&lt;/strong&gt; proven experience in a retail or fashion company with a store network and multi-channel model, and a solid command of store economics, seasonality, markdowns, inventory and open-to-buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full P&amp;amp;L vision:&lt;/strong&gt; hands-on experience owning or co-owning a full P&amp;amp;L, from top line to EBITDA, including consolidation across channels or countries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong margin expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; gross margin building blocks, markdown and promotional impact, landed cost, inventory valuation and provisions, with the ability to explain margin drivers clearly to non-finance stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous and process-oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; a track record of building or improving planning, closing and reporting processes, with reliable delivery against deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel / Google Sheets and financial modeling skills; experience with an ERP (NetSuite is a plus) and a BI or reporting tool (Power BI, Looker, Tableau or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Finance, Business or Engineering, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English required (global scope, US HQ, international teams); professional proficiency in French preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills: able to turn complex analyses into concise, decision-oriented messages and to challenge senior operational stakeholders with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture. Expect generous time off (including RTT), flexible work, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Style Perks: &lt;/strong&gt;enjoy a generous employee discount and seasonal wardrobe allotments — so you can live the brand, not just represent it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING seeks to empower its employees by providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, Veteran status, or other legally protected characteristics. Diversity and inclusion is critical to our success as a global brand, and we seek to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is a Los Angeles-based fashion house founded in 2012 that blends elements of Scandinavian simplicity with American energy to offer modern wardrobe essentials for women seeking a timeless yet rebellious approach to everyday style. Since its launch, ANINE BING has evolved into a global brand, available in over 90 countries with a growing network of brick-and-mortar retail stores in key cities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Powered by a global team of over 250 employees, ANINE BING is headquartered in Los Angeles and Paris, with additional offices in New York and Shanghai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Our Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located just off the Champs-Élysées, our Paris headquarters at 1 Rue François 1er is a cornerstone of our international growth. As the home of our Product teams and other key functions, this space reflects our commitment to creativity, collaboration, and global perspective. As we continue to grow across Europe, our Paris office plays a central role in shaping the future of our brand.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Why At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&amp;nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform – best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&amp;nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an SDET to join one of our agile engineering teams and help us build quality into LUMA, our scientific software platform. You&#39;ll take ownership of testing for a specific module of the application — writing and maintaining automated tests, exploring new features, and working alongside developers, application scientists and DevOps engineers to make sure what we ship is reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on automation role with room to grow. You&#39;ll be contributing to established test frameworks rather than building them from scratch, with support from senior SDETs who will help you develop your technical depth and your understanding of the science behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While the primary focus is automation, the role also involves manual exploratory testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;In this role you will get to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, maintain and extend automated test suites for your module using Cucumber, TypeScript and Cypress (and Playwright where we use it).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own day-to-day quality for your area: contributing test scenarios during planning, testing stories as they&#39;re built, and giving the team a clear picture of release readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and document test cases that cover functional, regression and integration scenarios, and keep them useful as the product evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and reproduce defects, raise well-evidenced bug reports in JIRA, and verify fixes with developers and scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep your tests green and trustworthy in our CI pipelines, and help improve how tests run and report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn to read and interpret API documentation and turn it into meaningful automated coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leading experts in software development, scientific product management and test automation — and be mentored by them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have &lt;strong&gt;2–5 years&#39; experience in QA/testing, including at least a year of hands-on test automation&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;re comfortable working in a code-first way, you enjoy digging into how things work, and you&#39;re happy asking questions when a domain is unfamiliar. You work carefully and pay attention to detail, and you can take a story or module, understand it and devise a concrete approach to testing going above and beyond the standard acceptance criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just as importantly, you want to get better. We&#39;re looking for someone who takes feedback well, is curious about the scientific problems our users are solving and wants to grow into a senior automation engineer over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Key Skills we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical experience with Cypress&lt;/strong&gt; — writing tests, using selectors and custom commands, debugging failures, and working within an existing Page Object Model. Experience testing React applications is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working knowledge of TypeScript or JavaScript&lt;/strong&gt;, including asynchronous code (promises, async/await). You don&#39;t need to be an expert in generics and interfaces, but you should be able to read and write clean, maintainable test code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with BDD / Cucumber&lt;/strong&gt;, or a willingness to pick it up quickly — we write most of our specs in Gherkin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test case design and documentation&lt;/strong&gt; — the ability to break a feature down into clear, repeatable scenarios and write them up so others can follow them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with Git and GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;, including branching, pull requests and code review, plus experience working in JIRA or a similar tracking system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Playwright, or interest in learning it — we use it for a subset of our tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to API testing tools (Postman, REST clients) or writing API-level automated tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Any experience with performance or load testing (K6 or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Familiarity with validating data integrity across release upgrades, migrations or schema changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;A background or interest in science, engineering or research software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Research shows us the&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;confidence gap&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;imposter syndrome can get in the way of meeting outstanding candidates, so please don’t hesitate to apply — we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree that Dotmatics may collect your personal data for recruiting, global organization planning, and related purposes. Dotmatics &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.dotmatics.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; explains what personal information we may process, where we may process your personal information, our purposes for processing your personal information, and the rights you can exercise over Dotmatics use of your personal information.&lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dotmatics is an equal opportunity employer. We are a welcoming place for everyone, and we do our best to make sure all people feel supported and connected at work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – E-Commerce Web Upper Funnel [CDI] (f/m/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localisation :&lt;/strong&gt; Paris ou Lille, France&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Équipe :&lt;/strong&gt; Decathlon E-Commerce Web – Périmètre Upper Funnel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos de l&#39;équipe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l&#39;écosystème digital mondial de Decathlon, notre équipe &lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Web&lt;/strong&gt; façonne la destination en ligne de millions de passionné·es de sport à travers le monde. Le périmètre &lt;strong&gt;Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt; constitue la porte d&#39;entrée de notre expérience digitale : de la page d&#39;accueil et la navigation par catégories, à la découverte de produits via le moteur de recherche, les recommandations IA, le commerce conversationnel, les espaces Retail Media et les contenus d&#39;inspiration. Notre mission est de guider de manière fluide chaque utilisateur de l&#39;inspiration jusqu&#39;à l&#39;intention d&#39;achat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rejoindre cette organisation Produit Web à fort trafic, c&#39;est évoluer à très grande échelle, où la vitesse, l&#39;excellence de la découverte, le SEO, la monétisation ciblée et les parcours personnalisés de nouvelle génération génèrent notre impact business quotidien.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;, tu apporteras la vision stratégique, l&#39;architecture fonctionnelle et le leadership produit nécessaires pour faire passer l&#39;expérience de découverte et d&#39;exploration de notre plateforme web à l&#39;échelle supérieure. En toute autonomie, tu traiteras des enjeux complexes : performance de la recherche, structuration du catalogue, intégration du Retail Media et virages technologiques de l&#39;IA (interfaces conversationnelles, agents autonomes).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tes responsabilités s&#39;articulent autour de 4 piliers stratégiques :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Alignement stratégique, gestion des parties prenantes &amp;amp; Vision Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Porter la vision globale de la découverte &amp;amp; de l&#39;engagement&lt;/strong&gt; : Définir et piloter la feuille de route stratégique des points de contact de l&#39;Upper Funnel (Page d&#39;accueil, Pages catégories/listes, Moteur de recherche, Arborescence/Taxonomie, Emplacements publicitaires Retail Media, Assistants conversationnels et Hubs d&#39;inspiration).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignement exécuteur &amp;amp; transversal&lt;/strong&gt; : Collaborer étroitement avec la direction business globale, les responsables merchandising, les spécialistes SEO, les équipes de monétisation Retail Media et la tech IA pour aligner l&#39;organisation sur les évolutions majeures de la plateforme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pilotage des métriques macro &amp;amp; performance du funnel&lt;/strong&gt; : Suivre et optimiser les métriques clés tout au long du parcours : Trafic organique/direct, CTR de la recherche, profondeur de navigation, taux d&#39;engagement conversationnel, rendement publicitaire (eCPM), taux de rebond, CTR vers les fiches produits (PDP) et conversion globale du haut de funnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Architecture fonctionnelle &amp;amp; Orchestration de l&#39;écosystème Web&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecte Fonctionnel·le Principal·e&lt;/strong&gt; : Définir la répartition des périmètres entre les squads web (&lt;em&gt;Search &amp;amp; Conversational Discovery, Taxonomy &amp;amp; Merchandising, Personalization/Recommendations, Retail Media &amp;amp; Sponsored Listings&lt;/em&gt;) afin d&#39;éliminer les frictions et les doublons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration étroite en Triade&lt;/strong&gt; : Travailler en synergie avec les Staff/Principal Web Engineers et les Staff UX/UI Designers pour aligner la performance frontend (Core Web Vitals), le Design System web, l&#39;architecture micro-frontend, les composants UI conversationnels et les API de recherche/ad-serving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parcours omnicanal &amp;amp; passage de relais fluide&lt;/strong&gt; : Garantir des transitions fluides depuis les canaux d&#39;acquisition externes vers l&#39;Upper Funnel web, en équilibrant la découverte organique, l&#39;assistance conversationnelle/agentique et les inventaires sponsorisés, tout en facilitant le passage vers le bas de funnel (PDP, Panier &amp;amp; Checkout).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Sparring stratégique &amp;amp; De-risking Produit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partenaire et mentor stratégique&lt;/strong&gt; : Conseiller les Group Product Managers (GPM) et Product Managers (PM) du domaine E-Commerce web pour naviguer au sein des algorithmes de recherche complexes, des architectures d&#39;agents LLM, des intégrations d&#39;ad-servers et des contraintes web à très fort volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stratégies de réduction des risques (De-risking)&lt;/strong&gt; : Formuler et exécuter des boucles de validation rapides sur les concepts à forte incertitude (recherche visuelle/vocale, conseillers produits conversationnels, réapprovisionnement/bundles agentiques, placements sponsorisés).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérimentation continue à grande échelle&lt;/strong&gt; : Piloter des stratégies de A/B testing et tests multivariés à fort trafic, en équilibrant l&#39;intensité des interactions conversationnelles et la pression publicitaire face à la conversion organique (frameworks CRO, Opportunity Solution Trees - OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Élévation de la culture &amp;amp; des capacités Web modernes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership IA, Agentique &amp;amp; Monétisation&lt;/strong&gt; : Promouvoir l&#39;adoption des solutions IA cloud-natives (ex: Google Vertex AI), des frameworks conversationnels, des modes d&#39;achat agentiques et des fonctionnalités Retail Media pour amplifier à la fois l&#39;expérience utilisateur et les revenus de la plateforme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Élévation des pratiques Produit&lt;/strong&gt; : Accompagner la communauté PM vers les meilleures pratiques du web moderne (frameworks de discovery continue, optimisation de la performance technique web, décisions guidées par la donnée).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multiplicateur d&#39;impact&lt;/strong&gt; : Élever le niveau collectif de l&#39;organisation Produit en tant que leader d&#39;opinion, sans rôle de management hiérarchique direct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience E-Commerce Web à échelle (7 ans+)&lt;/strong&gt; : Solide parcours en Product Management dans la mise à l&#39;échelle de plateformes e-commerce web à fort trafic (Upper Funnel, Search, Merchandising ou Navigation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise Upper Funnel &amp;amp; SEO&lt;/strong&gt; : Compréhension approfondie des mécaniques de haut de funnel, du SEO technique, des moteurs de recherche internes, de la structuration de taxonomies et de l&#39;optimisation du taux de conversion (CRO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maîtrise de la Discovery &amp;amp; de l&#39;Analytics&lt;/strong&gt; : Pratique avancée de l&#39;analytics web (GA4/Amplitude/Contentsquare), de l&#39;A/B testing à fort volume, de la recherche utilisateur qualitative/quantitative et des Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture fonctionnelle&lt;/strong&gt; : Capacité à découper des problématiques complexes de catalogue, d&#39;ad-tech et d&#39;IA/search en stratégies d&#39;exécution claires (MVP/V0/V1).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication exécutive&lt;/strong&gt; : Excellence dans la traduction d&#39;architectures search/agentiques complexes, d&#39;enjeux de revenus Retail Media et de métriques UX en présentations synthétiques pour les dirigeants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Atouts &amp;amp; Compétences technologiques clés (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pluses&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; :&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Google Vertex AI&lt;/strong&gt; : Une expérience pratique de Google Vertex AI (pour le Search, les Recommandations ou le déploiement de modèles ML/LLM) est un atout majeur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Conversationnel &amp;amp; Agentique&lt;/strong&gt; : Une bonne compréhension ou expérience des interfaces IA conversationnelles (chat/voix) et des concepts de commerce agentique (résolution autonome d&#39;intention, agents IA orientés tâches) est un fort plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail Media &amp;amp; Monétisation&lt;/strong&gt; : Une expérience des concepts de Retail Media et de la gestion publicitaire (produits sponsorisés, intégration ad-server, arbitrage rendement vs UX) est un vrai plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posture &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; : Fort pouvoir d&#39;influence sans autorité hiérarchique, capacité à s&#39;épanouir dans l&#39;ambiguïté, esprit de collaboration en Triade et empathie pour accompagner les PMs plus juniors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE NOUS T&#39;OFFRONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organisation de travail hybride&lt;/strong&gt; (basé à Paris ou Lille), 2 jours de télétravail possible par semaine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Matériel haut de gamme fourni&lt;/strong&gt; en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;&lt;/li&gt;
