&lt;p&gt;📍London / Distributed (UK) | 💰 £86,100 - £101,300 (depending on experience) ➕ incentive awards tied to your performance |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tDAT6VxoqQM&quot;&gt;Hear from the team&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⭐ About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic, commercially minded, and data-driven &lt;strong&gt;Senior Strategy and Operations Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, who will be an individual contributor and help shape the future of Payments at Monzo. You’ll play a critical role in supporting the GM of Payments and the leadership team to define, measure, and drive our strategy - balancing long-term vision with the realities of day-to-day delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership, high-impact role, ideal for someone who thrives on solving complex problems, is fuelled by strategic thinking, and enjoys using data to bring clarity to ambiguity. You’ll move seamlessly between blue-sky thinking and tactical execution - one day modelling the impact of a new product bet, the next helping optimise how we run the collective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll bring a birds-eye view across Payments’s portfolio - ensuring our goals, investments, and initiatives line up coherently with each other and with Monzo’s broader mission. And you’ll be the connective tissue that keeps us operating effectively: tracking performance, surfacing insights, and making sure we’re focused on what really matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔑 You’ll play a key role by…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving strategic clarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Supporting the GM of Payments and leadership team in defining, tracking, and evolving Payments’s strategic direction to align with Monzo’s wider mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively dive into large, complex datasets to uncover insights, diagnose operational challenges, and independently design and implement scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translating data into action:&lt;/strong&gt; Building and maintaining data-informed views of performance across products, squads, and initiatives; using insights to inform priorities and trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partnering closely with Product, Engineering, Data and Design teams to bridge the gap between ideas and strategic business execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owning business performance rhythm:&lt;/strong&gt; Leading monthly business reviews, reporting, and governance materials to keep the collective aligned and accountable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping new opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Scoping new bets through market sizing, commercial modelling, partnerships evaluation, and budget/forecast analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Making the org more effective:&lt;/strong&gt; Optimising how we balance KTLO, BAU, and growth work; supporting resourcing and squad setup decisions across the collective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connecting the dots:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensuring consistent communication and alignment across Payment squads, and with other Monzo collectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale &amp;amp; Geographic Expansion:&lt;/strong&gt; Playing a pivotal role in scaling our lending book and supporting launch operations as we expand our Borrowing products into new geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bringing teams together:&lt;/strong&gt; Leading Payments All Hands, goals processes, and strategic forums that ensure cohesion and momentum across the collective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if you have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a deeply strategic mind, capable of seeing the bigger picture, thinking in systems, and anticipating future trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional Problem-Solving Skills: &lt;/strong&gt;Your “superpower” is solving complex problems with analytical rigor, commercial viability, and execution certainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability &amp;amp; Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re a self-starter who thrives in ambiguity, adept at navigating complex, rapidly evolving environments, and driven by impact and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Influencing Without Authority:&lt;/strong&gt; You have an exceptional ability to connect the dots across different parts of the business, foster collaboration, and drive alignment without authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re comfortable making trade-offs and prioritisation decisions based on data, business impact, and resource constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Rigour&lt;/strong&gt;: A strong analytical skillset with a proven track record of comfortably navigating large datasets to solve unstructured problems independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with highly technical teams such as Machine Learning and Data/Analytics Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; You’re motivated by improving how teams work - finding ways to make organisations more efficient, scalable, and focused on what matters most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌 What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 £86,100 - £101,300 (depending on experience) + incentive awards tied to your performance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📍 We&#39;re open to distributed working within the UK, with the expectation of working from the London office on occasional basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 £1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏡 We will set you up to work from home; all employees are given Macbooks and for fully remote workers we will provide extra support for your work-from-home setup.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➕ Plus lots more!&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;Read our full list of benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 The application journey has 4 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phone call with Recruiter (30 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial behavioural video call with Hiring Manager (45 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical interview (60 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solving interview (60 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our average process takes around 3–4 weeks, but we will always work around your availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. You can read them&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-NZ1 #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a rapidly evolving world, trust in AI depends on AI agents being grounded in fresh, verified real-world data. Search is the foundation that makes this possible. We are building an agent-native search platform designed specifically for AI systems rather than human users. Our product provides programmatic, low-latency, and observable search APIs that AI agents use to retrieve, filter, and reason over real-world information at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to build the rendering infrastructure behind a novel search engine designed for agentic AI. In this role, you will design systems that transform modern web applications into high&amp;nbsp;quality structured content for search and AI. You will work on browser rendering, JavaScript execution, and large-scale rendering infrastructure capable of processing billions of pages efficiently. Modern websites increasingly rely on client-side rendering, dynamic data loading, and complex application frameworks. Your work will ensure we can reliably render, understand, and extract valuable information while minimising cost &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;and latency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, your responsibility will be to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build large-scale rendering systems for modern web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop browser-based rendering infrastructure capable of executing complex JavaScript applications reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research how modern frontend frameworks render and deliver content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve rendering quality, completeness, and performance across diverse websites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise rendering cost, latency, resource utilisation, and throughput at internet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate rendering research into reliable production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 5+ years of experience as a software engineer working on production backend or&amp;nbsp;infrastructure systems and are an expert in several of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Browser Rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chromium rendering pipeline — DOM, Layout, Paint, and Compositing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript execution inside browsers and rendering lifecycle and page readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Headless browser execution and browser instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, or similar frameworks Modern Web Applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, and modern frontend architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server-side rendering (SSR), client-side rendering (CSR), and streaming rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Single-page applications (SPA) and Progressive Web Apps (PWA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resource loading, lazy loading, and modern JavaScript bundles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have experience with:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and operating high-throughput content processing pipelines at internet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems design and performance optimisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-source contributions or active involvement in the engineering community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conference talks or technical publications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We conduct coding interviews as part of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Payroll Specialist owns end-to-end Dutch payroll, operated in Nmbrs, and acts as the designated backup for the company’s other international payrolls. This role harmonizes, simplifies, and continuously improves payroll execution and payroll accounting across the company’s Dutch entities, pay groups, providers, and systems. This is to make sure payroll remains accurate, compliant, trusted, and understandable as the company grows without a proportional increase in manual work or risk. As international backup, the role maintains working proficiency in the company’s other country payrolls and provides continuity during peak periods, absences, and year-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end Dutch payroll execution in Nmbrs across entities and pay groups: monthly and off-cycle runs, holiday allowance, year-end close and annual statements (jaaropgaven), and the payroll calendar; define consistent execution standards that meet Dutch statutory and contractual requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Dutch payroll tax and social security compliance: wage tax and national insurance contributions (loonheffingen), employee insurance and Zvw premiums, the work-related costs scheme (WKR), timely and accurate loonaangifte to the Belastingdienst, corrections, and resolution of Belastingdienst and UWV correspondence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer regulated and complex pay items accurately: the 30% ruling and other expatriate and cross-border arrangements, equity income (RSU/option) taxation, pension contributions and provider files, sick leave and statutory leave schemes, transition payments and termination settlements, wage garnishments (loonbeslag), and taxable benefits-in-kind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and reconcile shadow payrolls in Nmbrs for internationally mobile employees (inbound assignees, cross-border and remote workers, and outbound Dutch employees with a host-country shadow payroll)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the designated backup for the company’s other international payrolls: maintain working knowledge of country calendars, providers, and controls, and run or support pay cycles during absences, peak periods, and year-end in coordination with the payroll owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause analysis for recurring payroll, accounting, or service failures; design and implement durable fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process harmonization and simplification to reduce manual steps, handoffs, rework, and off-cycle runs; make full use of Nmbrs functionality, integrations, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead payroll execution during transitions (new entity launches, provider or system changes, restructures/M&amp;amp;A), ensuring continuity and control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure payroll accounting remains clean as scope changes: consistent journals, accruals, reversals, and reconciliation standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor preventative controls by design, including SOX-aligned payroll controls; improve evidence pack quality and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as escalation owner for complex or sensitive pay issues; provide authoritative explanations to employees and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR Ops, Finance, Legal/Compliance, Nmbrs, and international payroll providers to deliver scalable operating models and service quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 7+ years of Dutch payroll experience, including multi-entity scope in complex environments (growth, change, or hybrid in-house/outsourced models).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on Nmbrs experience: running payroll end to end, configuring wage components and journal mappings, managing loonaangifte and corrections, and using its reporting and integrations (HRIS, GL, pension and benefits providers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of Dutch payroll compliance: loonheffingen and social security, WKR, the 30% ruling, expatriate taxation and shadow payroll, pension administration, sick leave and statutory leave, termination settlements, and year-end reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of international payroll (running or overseeing outsourced country payrolls) and readiness to act as the designated backup for the company’s other payrolls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong payroll controllership skills: ability to design controls, enforce SoD/approvals, and ensure audit-ready evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven capability improving payroll processes (standardization, automation enablement, reducing manual effort and errors) and leading transitions (vendor/system/new entity) with structured planning and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong payroll accounting knowledge and experience working with Finance during close and audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management; comfortable acting as an escalation owner and payroll authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English and professional working proficiency in Dutch (statutory correspondence, legislation, and provider documentation are in Dutch).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dutch payroll qualification (PDL and/or VPS) and/or Nmbrs certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with international payroll providers or aggregators and multi-country operating models (SLAs, KPIs, remediation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating payroll controls in a SOX-compliant, US-listed company environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with equity compensation payroll (RSUs/options), including cross-border cases and trailing tax liabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Global Mobility programs: shadow payroll set-up, tax equalization/protection and hypothetical tax, gross-ups, and year-end assignee reconciliations with tax advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
